    {"content":"<h1>How to Pass Creación Digital II</h1><h2>Universidad Europea · UEM 2026-27</h2><p><strong>Rubén Vega Balbás, PhD</strong></p><p><em>6 ECTS · 150 h · 80 h contact</em></p><p>Final event theme: <strong>Communicate and inspire: What is fashion for you?</strong></p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Official weights (unchanged)</h2><p>Follow the UEM guía table for this subject. Studio choreography maps onto those instruments — it does not rewrite them.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Every session (order binding)</h2><ol><li><strong>Analysis strip</strong> — sessions 1–2: modelled analysis; from session 3: <strong>2×15 min</strong> student defences</li><li><strong>Masterclass</strong> — ideas + images</li><li><strong>Lab (Portfolio)</strong> — exercises → portfolio</li><li><strong>Workshop (Deliverable)</strong> — next deliverable clock</li></ol><p><em>Lab ≠ Workshop.</em></p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Slide rule</h2><p>Geometrical slide before Lab: exercises are portfolio-bound. Geometrical Workshop open + outro. Masterclass uses accepted media packs.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Five deliverables</h2><ol><li><strong>D1 Analysis</strong> — defence slideshow · Madrid exhibition fashion image</li><li><strong>D2 Transposition</strong> — into an image · critical review / circulation</li><li><strong>D3 Atrium</strong> — tech script + live · <em>What is fashion for you?</em></li><li><strong>D4 Portfolio index</strong></li><li><strong>D5 Exam</strong> — test + self-review of process</li></ol>"},
    {"content":"<h2>II.5 note</h2><p>Web/portfolio craft supports D4. A public showroom URL is optional and requires the exhibition gate.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Consent and dates</h2><p>Private/local artefacts OK for teaching. Public exhibition OFF until consent and administration. Dates: guía + Campus Virtual.</p>","calendar_note":true},
